## Every invariant of the spec, by id
A file may cite another invariant by id; for `one_owner` and `terms_defined_once`, an id here
that names the owner of a decision is enough: do not fail an item because that invariant is not
shown.
{% for i in additionalContext.index %}{{ i }}
{% endfor %}
## How to answer
Walk the files in order and answer every item for each; do not stop at the first failing item.
An item fails only for a concrete reason you can quote: the words at fault and, for every item
but `mentions_complete`, an input or a reading that two careful readers would decide differently
or that breaks the rule the item names. Do not fail an item to ask for a rewording of a text that
already says one thing, nor for what an entity's doc already settles when the file reads it as
the doc defines it.
